Breaks:
 postgresql-PG_MAJOR_VERSION-safesession,
Description: read-only session enforcement for PostgreSQL roles
 pgEdge SafeSession is a PostgreSQL extension that enforces read-only
 sessions for specified database roles, using executor and utility hooks to
 block DML, DDL, COPY FROM, GRANT/REVOKE, VACUUM/ANALYZE and volatile
 C-language function execution.
 .
 The module must be listed in shared_preload_libraries and the restricted
 roles configured through pgedge_safesession.roles before enforcement takes
 effect.
